  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZigZag Solar: Illuminating India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In large Indian cities like Chenai and Bangalore consistent supply of electricity is often challenged by power black-outs and heavy rainfall, leading to the use of improvised and often dangerous and polluting energy sources in Indian households such as batteries, coal and motorised energy generation. Wallvision developed an innovative architectural fa&#xe7;ade technology to harvest solar power called ZigZagsolar. It vertically installs solar panels and enables the use of facades and walls of buildings for solar energy generation. In order to introduce ZigZagSolar to the Indian market and to prepare for future investments, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provides support for a pilot project in India to demonstrate the facades. The project includes developing a supply chain, identifying suppliers, distributors, agents and installers and the development a profit model. Although the key objective of the project is to validate and introduce the technology in the Indian market, the project currently already supports 3 direct jobs and 20 indirect jobs. Upon successful validation, further investments in the set-up of a local subsidiary, R&amp;D centre and local manufacturing will be explored and will contribute to the development of unique skills, knowledge transfer and new jobs for the Indian market. Furthermore the project aims to contribute to a greener world and to transform India by curbing black outs, reducing the use of dangerous and unsustainable energy sources, contributing to electrification and cleaner air in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
